T1  - A group-mediated cognitive-behavioral intervention for increasing adherence to physical activity in older adults.
A1  - Brawley, Lawrence R
A1  - Rejeski, W. Jack
A1  - Lutes, Lesley

Y1  - 2000//
N2  - Examined the efficacy of a group-mediated cognitive behavioral intervention (GMCB) on adherence rates to physically active lifestyles in older adults. 60 older adults (aged 65-78 yrs) were randomized to 1 of 3 groups: waiting list control, a standard physical activity program (SPA), or GMCB. The SPA and GMCB involved 6 mo of combined center- and home-based activity. Contact with Ss was then terminated with a follow-up assessment at 9 mo. Results revealed that, at the 9-mo follow-up the GMCB group had a higher frequency of weekly physical activity than the SPA group. At 6 mo, both groups were more active, had higher aerobic power, and improved health-related quality of life when compared with the control group. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2022 APA, all rights reserved)
